<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Italian Somaliland</h1><p class="st-meta">1889 CE – 1941 CE · capital Mogadishu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Italy's colony in southern and north-eastern Somalia, the launch pad for the invasion of Ethiopia in 1935 and later part of Italian East Africa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1888 and 1889 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> treaties with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-hobyo">Sultanate of Hobyo</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/majeerteen-sultanate">Majeerteen Sultanate</a>. In 1892 it leased the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benadir">Benadir</a> ports, including <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marka">Merca</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barawa">Barawa</a>, from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Sultanate of Zanzibar</a>, administering them at first through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartered-company">chartered companies</a>. The Italian state took direct control in 1905 and bought the ports outright.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Italian rule spread slowly inland. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jubaland">Jubaland</a> in 1924 and under the Fascist governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-maria-de-vecchi">Cesare De Vecchi</a> the northern sultanates were conquered by 1927. Italian concessions developed banana and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> plantations along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shebelle-river">Shabelle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jubba-river">Jubba</a> rivers, often with forced labour. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a> gained Italian-style buildings, among them a cathedral, now destroyed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walwal-incident">Walwal incident</a> of 1934 became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy's</a> pretext for invading <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, and in 1936 the colony became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a>. British forces occupied it in 1941. In 1950 Italy returned as administrator of the UN <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-somaliland">Trust Territory of Somaliland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/italian-somaliland.jpg" alt="Italian Somaliland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy_(1861-1946)_crowned.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1889 CE – 1941 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mogadishu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cesare De Vecchi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Somalia Italiana, Italian Somalia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1915&amp;focus=italian-somaliland" aria-label="Italian Somaliland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5939 2101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Italian Somaliland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6259 2357L6253 2354M6259 2357L6413 2045M6259 2357L6345 2233M6259 2357L6173 1949M6259 2357L6070 2096M6259 2357L6259 2357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6253 2354h0M6413 2045h0M6345 2233h0M6173 1949h0M6070 2096h0M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6259 2357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mogadishu. <a href="/atlas?year=1915&amp;focus=italian-somaliland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
